WEBVTT

1
00:00:09.070 --> 00:00:11.692
Claudia hurried into the local TV station.

2
00:00:12.712 --> 00:00:18.256
As her prize for winning a local journalism contest, she was going to follow a TV news reporter

3
00:00:18.316 --> 00:00:19.457
for the entire day.

4
00:00:19.477 --> 00:00:22.679
"This is going to be awesome!"

5
00:00:23.060 --> 00:00:23.540
she thought.

6
00:00:26.502 --> 00:00:28.784
The first part of the day was a morning meeting.

7
00:00:29.720 --> 00:00:33.602
Claudia listened as the news director assigned news stories to reporters.

8
00:00:34.982 --> 00:00:38.664
Afterward, a reporter named Meredith Burke approached Claudia.

9
00:00:38.684 --> 00:00:40.905
"You'll be working with me today."

10
00:00:42.725 --> 00:00:45.747
Claudia forced a smile as she shook Meredith's hand.

11
00:00:46.627 --> 00:00:52.630
The reporter seemed very smart, but Claudia had been hoping to work with a reporter covering something exciting.

12
00:00:53.490 --> 00:00:57.972
Meredith had been assigned to a story with a boring topic—road repairs.

13
00:00:59.036 --> 00:01:02.258
Meredith led Claudia over to her desk and reached for a phone.

14
00:01:02.278 --> 00:01:08.822
"First we have to schedule interviews with people who might be affected by the construction.

15
00:01:10.803 --> 00:01:15.405
You might be surprised to learn that a TV reporter spends a lot of time on the phone.

16
00:01:17.246 --> 00:01:19.027
Do you have any questions about the story?"

17
00:01:20.528 --> 00:01:21.789
Claudia shook her head.

18
00:01:22.729 --> 00:01:26.812
She didn't feel interested enough in road construction to have any questions.

19
00:01:27.856 --> 00:01:32.619
Still, she tried to act polite and listen alertly as the reporter made the calls.

20
00:01:33.840 --> 00:01:35.140
Finally Meredith hung up.

21
00:01:36.281 --> 00:01:39.683
"I've arranged to meet with some people in the area near the project.

22
00:01:41.284 --> 00:01:44.265
Let's find Jeremy, my videographer, and get in the van."

23
00:01:44.285 --> 00:01:48.928
"Sounds good," Claudia mumbled.

24
00:01:50.909 --> 00:01:55.652
At the roadwork site, Claudia saw construction workers and large vehicles everywhere.

25
00:01:58.536 --> 00:02:00.237
"What do you think we should record, Claudia?"

26
00:02:00.777 --> 00:02:01.678
Meredith asked.

27
00:02:01.698 --> 00:02:05.460
"Aren't you going to interview people?"

28
00:02:05.821 --> 00:02:06.701
Claudia asked.

29
00:02:08.902 --> 00:02:11.964
"Yes, but we need to record more than just the interviews."

30
00:02:12.905 --> 00:02:13.785
Jeremy nodded.

31
00:02:13.805 --> 00:02:20.189
"It would be pretty boring to show people talking about roadwork without showing the actual construction."

32
00:02:21.470 --> 00:02:24.452
Claudia looked around as Jeremy began setting up his camera.

33
00:02:28.048 --> 00:02:31.531
"Well, maybe you could film around the whole construction site?

34
00:02:33.012 --> 00:02:35.633
And also get some close-ups of the road?"

35
00:02:36.594 --> 00:02:37.575
Meredith smiled.

36
00:02:37.595 --> 00:02:40.036
"Smart ideas."

37
00:02:41.477 --> 00:02:44.299
She began giving more specific directions to Jeremy.

38
00:02:45.180 --> 00:02:50.964
News stories on TV were usually only a couple of minutes long—but Jeremy recorded for much longer than

39
00:02:51.024 --> 00:02:56.288
that. "We'll edit everything back at the TV station," Meredith explained.

40
00:02:57.724 --> 00:02:59.345
"Now it's time to interview some people.

41
00:03:00.886 --> 00:03:02.266
What questions should I ask?"

42
00:03:02.286 --> 00:03:06.028
"Um Claudia thought.

43
00:03:06.048 --> 00:03:08.949
"Are you happy with the roadwork?"

44
00:03:10.290 --> 00:03:11.710
"That's an okay way to start.

45
00:03:13.491 --> 00:03:16.733
But yes or no questions aren't very exciting for interviews.

46
00:03:18.133 --> 00:03:22.875
What about—" "How do you feel about the roadwork?"

47
00:03:23.195 --> 00:03:24.296
Claudia burst out.

48
00:03:25.684 --> 00:03:28.226
Meredith grinned and showed Claudia her notepad.

49
00:03:29.126 --> 00:03:30.967
"That's actually my first question!"

50
00:03:33.269 --> 00:03:38.372
Throughout the morning Claudia observed as Meredith interviewed local residents and business owners.

51
00:03:40.993 --> 00:03:43.414
Everyone had an opinion on the construction.

52
00:03:43.435 --> 00:03:49.418
"I'm glad the city is finally repairing the roads," one woman said.

53
00:03:49.438 --> 00:03:52.460
"It will improve my commute."

54
00:03:53.824 --> 00:03:57.067
"We can't ride our bikes anymore," a kid complained.

55
00:03:57.087 --> 00:04:00.850
"And our bus stop got moved to a different street!"

56
00:04:00.870 --> 00:04:06.535
"The construction is terrible for business," a restaurant owner said.

57
00:04:06.555 --> 00:04:12.460
"I think this is enough," Meredith said after her sixth interview.

58
00:04:12.480 --> 00:04:16.564
"Now we need to record an introduction to the story.

59
00:04:18.864 --> 00:04:23.325
After seeing the site and doing some interviews, I think I know how to report the story to

60
00:04:23.365 --> 00:04:28.527
viewers." Meredith and Jeremy planned out a few shots.

61
00:04:29.487 --> 00:04:31.948
Then she stood in front of the camera with a microphone.

62
00:04:31.968 --> 00:04:42.210
"Local residents have mixed reactions to roadwork on Renard Road Back at the station, Meredith led Claudia to

63
00:04:42.250 --> 00:04:44.071
an editing room with computer monitors.

64
00:04:44.091 --> 00:04:47.852
"We recorded about two hours of material.

65
00:04:49.968 --> 00:04:53.029
Now we're going to edit it down to a two-minute segment."

66
00:04:55.210 --> 00:04:57.650
Meredith showed Claudia how the software worked.

67
00:04:58.750 --> 00:05:04.532
After she'd finished the video segment, she recorded a few more lines of sound in a recording booth.

68
00:05:04.552 --> 00:05:12.494
"Finished!" "That was a ton of work for a two-minute story," Claudia said.

69
00:05:12.514 --> 00:05:15.115
"But it was really fun."

70
00:05:15.135 --> 00:05:18.696
"Phew!" Meredith looked relieved.

71
00:05:20.212 --> 00:05:23.175
"I was afraid you might find a story about roadwork boring."

72
00:05:23.195 --> 00:05:28.099
"Maybe at first," Claudia admitted.

73
00:05:28.119 --> 00:05:32.423
"But it certainly matters to the people in that neighborhood."

74
00:05:33.544 --> 00:05:36.147
"Ready to see if the news desk has another story for us?"

75
00:05:36.747 --> 00:05:37.648
Meredith asked.

76
00:05:39.350 --> 00:05:41.912
"Reporters usually handle several stories in a day."

77
00:05:43.994 --> 00:05:46.056
Claudia was already on her feet.
